        "original_id": "8d13d56f-dd97-5dff-8f09-a1df732442f1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Asiniiwin, Rocky Boy, Stone Child\n- Places: Rocky Boy's Indian Reservation, Montana, Hill County, Chouteau County, Canada–U.S. border\n- Organizations: Montana Chippewa-Cree\n- Topics: American Indian reservations\n\nFacts:\n- Asiniiwin, translated as Rocky Boy or Stone Child, was an important Chippewa leader.\n- Asiniiwin became the principal leader of the Montana Chippewa-Cree in the late 19th century and early 20th century.\n- Rocky Boy's Indian Reservation is one of seven American Indian reservations in Montana.\n- Rocky Boy's Indian Reservation is located in Hill and Chouteau counties in northeastern Montana, about 40 miles from the Canada–U.S. border.",
